\begin_layout Chapter
Additional Views and Interfaces
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Additional Eclipse Views in Bio7
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Some views of the Eclipse platform are available in Bio7 (
\series bold
Window > Show View
\series default
):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Bookmarks
\series default
 view shows the bookmarks of all editors to easily find points in code which have to be edited.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Tasks
\series default
 view shows the tasks (e.g., TODO comments) of the editors with priorities.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Problems
\series default
 view shows the errors and warnings of the compiler and of the code analysis of the editors.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Progress
\series default
 view shows the running jobs (e.g., Python scripts and the installation of packages) with a stop button. It can also be opened with the progress indicator of the status line.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Properties
\series default
 view shows the properties of a selected resource.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Error Log
\series default
 view shows the messages and errors of the platform.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
The LLM Assistant
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:LLM-Assistant"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\series bold
LLM Assistant
\series default
 is a chat with a large language model (LLM) which helps with the analysis of images and the writing of code. It is a plugin of SWTImageJ which is installed by default: 
\series bold
Plugins > LLM Assistant > Chat...
\series default
 in the ImageJ menu opens the chat, which Bio7 docks as the view 
\series bold
LLM Assistant
\series default
 (
\series bold
Open as Window
\series default
 in the toolbar of the view opens it as a window). The assistant works with servers which are compatible with the OpenAI API (e.g., OpenAI, OpenRouter, or local servers like LM Studio and Ollama). In 
\series bold
Plugins > LLM Assistant > General Preferences...
\series default
 the API keys (or the environment variable 
\family typewriter
OPENAI_API_KEY
\family default
; local servers need no key), the base URL and the default model are set (
\series bold
Test connection
\series default
 checks the connection). 
\series bold
Documents...
\series default
 manages documents for the context of the chat. The assistant can write code into the editors of Bio7: new files are created in the project 
\family typewriter
LLM_Code
\family default
 of the workspace, 
\series bold
Remove Code Tool Markers
\series default
 in the editor removes the markers of the assistant.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Java Libraries (Maven and the Dynamic Classpath)
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Java-Libraries"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Java code in Bio7 (the embedded Java compiler, the Java editor, the scripts and the GUIs) can use additional Java libraries (*.jar files), e.g., a chart library, a database driver or an image processing library. The libraries are managed in 
\series bold
Preferences Bio7 > Preferences Java Dynamic Compilation > Preferences Libraries
\series default
. They can be added as files or downloaded with their dependencies from Maven Central.
\end_layout

