\begin_layout Subsection
Code Completion: Fix Project Classpath
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Fix-Project-Classpath"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Java editor (code completion, imports, error markers) uses the classpath of the Java project. New Java projects which are created with the Bio7 wizards contain the libraries of the preferences automatically. After a library has been added (or removed), the classpath of an existing project has to be recalculated: select the Java project in the Project Explorer and choose 
\series bold
Fix Project Classpath
\series default
 in its context menu. Bio7 sets the classpath of the project to the bundled JDK, the libraries of Bio7 and the added libraries and confirms "Java Bio7 Project Libraries Recalculated!". Then the classes of the new library are proposed by the code completion and can be imported (e.g., 
\family typewriter
import org.jfree.chart.JFreeChart;
\family default
).
\end_layout

