\begin_layout Section
Java and Script Interaction with R and Python
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Java (compiled with the embedded compiler) and the script languages of Bio7 (Groovy, BeanShell, JavaScript) can use the embedded R and the embedded Python directly: values are transferred without files or sockets. In this way, e.g., GUIs can be created in Java which evaluate R or Python code, models can use statistical methods of R or Python, and the R and Python methods can be combined with the API of ImageJ.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
R (class 
\family typewriter
com.eco.bio7.rbridge.RUtil
\family default
):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\family typewriter
RUtil.isAlive()
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
RUtil.exec(code)
\family default
 (evaluate) and 
\family typewriter
RUtil.eval(code)
\family default
 (evaluate and return the value as an 
\family typewriter
RValue
\family default
), 
\family typewriter
RUtil.print(code)
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Java to R: 
\family typewriter
RUtil.toR(name, values)
\family default
 (double, int, String and boolean values or a double matrix), 
\family typewriter
dataFrameToR
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
listToR
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
imageToR
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
R to Java: 
\family typewriter
fromRDoubles
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromRDouble
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromRInts
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromRStrings
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromRString
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromRMatrix
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromRList
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
imageFromR
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Python (class 
\family typewriter
com.eco.bio7.pybridge.PythonUtil
\family default
):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\family typewriter
PythonUtil.isAlive()
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
PythonUtil.start()
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
PythonUtil.exec(code)
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
PythonUtil.eval(code)
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
PythonUtil.run(file)
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Java to Python: 
\family typewriter
toPython(name, values)
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
imageToPython
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
resultsTableToPython
\family default
; Python to Java: 
\family typewriter
fromPython
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
fromPythonDoubles
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
imageFromPython
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Between Python and R: 
\family typewriter
pythonToR(pythonExpression, rName)
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
rToPython(rExpression, pythonName)
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\family typewriter
PythonCalls.register(name, function)
\family default
 registers a Java function which Python calls with 
\family typewriter
bio7.call(name, ...)
\family default
. Python itself calls the Java API with 
\family typewriter
bio7.java
\family default
 (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:The-Python-Perspective"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

