\begin_layout Section
LibreOffice Features of Bio7
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:LibreOffice-features-of"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If LibreOffice is installed (the path is set in 
\series bold
Preferences Bio7
\series default
, 
\series bold
Path to LibreOffice
\series default
), data can be exchanged with the spreadsheet of LibreOffice. The actions are in the context menu of the R-Shell view, submenu 
\series bold
LibreOffice
\series default
:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
\series bold
Open LibreOffice Connection
\series default
 starts LibreOffice and connects it with Bio7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
\series bold
Open Spreadsheet
\series default
 opens a new spreadsheet. The spreadsheet can be filled by hand or with data from a file (in LibreOffice: 
\series bold
Sheet > Insert Sheet from File
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
\series bold
Data to R
\series default
 transfers the selected cells to the R workspace (the columns as lists and the selected values as a data frame).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
\series bold
Data with Head to R
\series default
 transfers numeric values with a head (the column names) to R.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Table view imports and exports LibreOffice spreadsheets, too (
\series bold
Import LibreOffice (ODS)
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Export as LibreOffice (ODS)
\series default
 in its File menu). A small API for the data transfer with LibreOffice is demonstrated in the script examples (LibreOffice_Snippets).
\end_layout


